  1. DEFINITIONS
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------

  "Affiliate" means an entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under
  common control with a party.

  "Authorized Deployment" means a single production installation of the
  Software operated by or on behalf of Licensee, plus any non-production
  environments (development, staging, preview) reasonably required to support
  that production installation.

  "Client-Facing Material" means any report, proposal, roadmap, or other
  deliverable generated by the Software that is intended to be shared with or
  shown to Licensee's clients or prospects.

  "Derivative Work" means any work, whether in source or object form, that is
  based on or derived from the Software and that would, under applicable
  copyright law, require a license from the Licensor — including modifications,
  extensions, localizations, integrations, and embedded copies.

  "Internal Use" means use by Licensee's personnel and contractors (acting in
  their capacity for Licensee) within Licensee's own business operations,
  excluding any redistribution or resale of the Software itself.

  "Licensor" means the repository owner of WinterVell and its Affiliates.

  "Production Deployment" means an installation of the Software that serves
  real end users, clients, or prospects in a live, non-demo capacity.

  "Source Code" means the human-readable form of the Software, including
  build scripts, configuration templates, schemas, and documentation.

